            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Walmart earnings, EV latest, Fed eyes tariff impacts: ICYMI",
            "description": "<p>The action never stops for Wall Street investors and top economists. Here's a brief recap in case you missed any of the week's big headlines.</p>\n<p>Walmart (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/WMT\">WMT</a>) shares declined after the retail giant beat fourth quarter earnings estimates while issuing cautious guidance. Learn more here:</p>\n<p><a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/walmart-earnings-retailer-well-positioned-160500313.html\"><strong>Walmart earnings: Retailer 'well-positioned' for a beat-and-raise</strong></a></p>\n<p>EV maker Nikola (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/NKLA\">NKLA</a>) filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy, while Rivian (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/RIVN\">RIVN</a>) released its latest quarterly results. Learn more here:</p>\n<p><a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/rivians-weak-sales-outlook-shows-151832795.html\"><strong>Rivian's weak sales outlook shows 'real demand issue' for EVs</strong></a></p>\n<p><a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/tesla-look-nissan-opportunity-analyst-155441306.html\"><strong>Tesla 'should take a look' at Nissan opportunity, analyst says</strong></a></p>\n<p><a data-i13n=\"cpos:7;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/nikola-files-chapter-11-bankruptcy-161930970.html\"><strong>Nikola files for Chapter 11 bankruptcy. EV stock nosedives.</strong></a></p>\n<p>Yahoo Finance heard from an array of Wall Street experts and Federal Reserve Bank of Atlanta President Raphael Bostic this week over how the central bank is viewing the tariff impacts on inflation. Learn more here:</p>\n<p><a data-i13n=\"cpos:8;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/trump-admin-trying-bring-down-153834841.html\"><strong>How the Trump admin. is trying to bring down yields</strong></a></p>\n<p><a data-i13n=\"cpos:9;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/tariff-uncertainty-destabilizing-consumers-companies-231000379.html\"><strong>Tariff uncertainty is 'destabilizing' for consumers and companies</strong></a></p>\n<p><a data-i13n=\"cpos:10;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/short-term-investing-creating-capital-121549181.html\"><strong>Short-term investing: Creating capital appreciation through bonds</strong></a></p>\n<p><a data-i13n=\"cpos:11;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/consumers-tapped-further-price-hikes-212159747.html\"><strong>Consumers are 'tapped out' on further price hikes: Fed's Bostic</strong></a></p>\n<p>For more expert insight and the latest market action, click\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:12;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/?fr=sycsrp_catchall\">here</a>.</p>\n<p><em>This post was written by </em><a data-i13n=\"cpos:13;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/luke-carberry-mogan/\"><em>Luke Carberry Mogan</em></a><em>.</em></p>",
            "summary": "The action never stops for Wall Street investors and top economists. Here's a brief recap in case you missed any of the week's big headlines. Walmart (WMT) shares declined after the retail giant beat fourth quarter earnings estimates while issuing cautious guidance. Learn more here: Walmart earnings: Retailer 'well-positioned' for a beat-and-raise EV maker Nikola (NKLA) filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy, while Rivian (RIVN) released its latest quarterly results. Learn more here: Rivian's weak sales outlook shows 'real demand issue' for EVs Tesla 'should take a look' at Nissan opportunity, analyst says Nikola files for Chapter 11 bankruptcy. EV stock nosedives. Yahoo Finance heard from an array of Wall Street experts and Federal Reserve Bank of Atlanta President Raphael Bostic this week over how the central bank is viewing the tariff impacts on inflation. Learn more here: How the Trump admin. is trying to bring down yields Tariff uncertainty is 'destabilizing' for consumers and companies Short-term investing: Creating capital appreciation through bonds Consumers are 'tapped out' on further price hikes: Fed's Bostic For more expert insight and the latest market action, click&nbsp;here. This post was written by Luke Carberry Mogan.",
